        <zone h='12407' id='14' name='Launch-Ready Replenishment Options | Operational &amp; Economic Comparison' w='75972' x='191' y='38368' />
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='19420' id='15' type-v2='text' w='75844' x='0' y='48146'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>EXECUTIVE DECISION SUMMARY</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12' italic='true'>Demand Surge</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>: Adding 276 units in Week 4 achieves a modeled 100% fill rate, eliminating 276 shortage units and reducing illustrative economic exposure by $16,888 versus no intervention.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12' italic='true'>Supplier Delay</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>: Expediting the original shipment achieves 100% fulfillment with $2,500 in illustrative economic exposure, compared with $8,420 for the Week 3 bridge alternative.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12' italic='true'>Recommendation</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>: Prioritize interventions that achieve the 98% launch-readiness threshold while minimizing modeled economic exposure. Results are based on hypothetical planning assumptions, and sensitivity analysis shows that readiness varies under changing operating conditions.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
